While the market already had decent AI harnesses, none of them felt like they had what I actually needed.&lt;p&gt;What began as a simple, minimalist tool quickly grew into one of my most ambitious projects. 
I started with basic tool calling and streaming, but that wasn't enough. I wanted a full-fledged application where I could build my own apps and that required testing and maturity.&lt;p&gt;I needed local artifacts where I could easily revert unwanted file changes, an editor to view and modify project files directly, a memory tab to review past prompts and code changes, and a practical agent system with skills so I wouldn't have to rewrite files just to add roles.&lt;p&gt;Nothing about ADDOM is perfect, but it's a solid foundation. It's been a lot of fun to play with. It’s MIT-licensed, open to contributions, and I hope you like it.&lt;p&gt;Thanks for taking the time to read this. Happy coding!
Check it out at &lt;a href="https://www.addom.app/" rel="nofollow"&gt;https://www.addom.app/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
